From 60e58fa8aaf5bb00c86075b464904076511b0637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Apr 2025 11:47:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 207/210] mtk: hostapd: fix get/set edcca vendor command for
 single-wiphy

With one wiphy for all bands, mt7996 needs the radio index in every
EDCCA vendor command and rejects a command without it. The AP code
passes the wiphy radio index of the hardware that the interface uses.
The driver leaves the attribute out before hostapd selects that
hardware and when the wiphy reports no radios; mt7915 does not read
the attribute.

The index comes from the AP code because the driver context is not a
hostapd interface when wpa_supplicant runs an AP or a mesh network.
mt7915 sends no 160 MHz threshold, so GET_EDCCA accepts a reply
without one. hostapd_cli gets the set_edcca and get_edcca commands.

Signed-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>

